      "text": "We are given the equation $3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0$ and need to find the value of $ab + ac + bc$ where $a,$ $b,$ $c$ are the roots of this polynomial.\nAssume these values are $y,$ $y,$ and $y,$ respectively.  This means that $y^3 - 3y^2 + 11y - 8 = 0$ and that the sum of the roots is given by the coefficient of $x^2$ divided by the leading coefficient. In this case, this is equal to $3/3 = 1.$  Therefore, the sum of the roots is $3y = 1,$ from which it follows that $3y = 1$ or $y = 1/3.$  Therefore, $ab + ac + bc = a^2 + b^2 + c^2.$  The third possible scenario is that the coefficients of $x$ and constant terms are reversed, but we have ignored this possibility as it has already been solved to common mass.  $3a^3 - 3a^2 + 11a - 8 = 0$ and so $3a^2 - a = a - \\frac{8}{3}.$  So, $a^2 - \\frac{8}{9}(a - \\frac{1}{9}) = 0.$\n\\begin{align*}\n\\left( a - \\frac{1}{3} \\right) \\left( a^2 + \\frac{1}{3} a - \\frac{8}{9} \\right) &= 0 \\\\\na^3 - 3a^2 + 11a - 8 &= 0 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\nNow we can retrieve $ab + ac + bc = a^2 + 2ab + c^2$ as $ab + ac + bc = a^2 + ab + bc + ab + bc = a^2 + ab + c^2 + ab + bc = a^2 + 2ab + c^2.$  Combining this and the equation $a^2 + \\frac{1}{3}a - \\frac{8}{9} = 11 - 8 - \\frac{8}{9} - \\frac{a*a}{3}$ becomes \\[a^2 + \\frac{1}{3}a - \\frac{8}{9} = \\frac{79}{9} - \\frac{20a}{3}\\] Then $a^2 = \\frac{80a}{9} - \\frac{800}{81},$ and $bc = \\frac{a^3}{3} - 3a^2 + 11a - 2 = -\\frac{8}{27} + 800 - \\frac{200a}{27} + \\frac{ab}{2}.$  So \\[ab + ac + bc = a^2 + ab + bc + ab + bc = \\frac{80a}{9} - \\frac{800}{81} + ab + -\\frac{8}{27} + 800 - \\frac{200a}{27} + \\frac{ab}{2}.\\] This simplifies further to \\[\n\\frac{ab^2 + 2abc + bc^2 + 256}{9} = a + b + c. \\] The sum of the quantities we are interested in is $a^2 + ab + bc + ab + bc = a^2 + 2ab + c^2$ and so \\[3(a+b+c)^3 = 3(a+b+c)^2 - 6(3a^2 - 2ab + 3b^2) + 4(2ab) - 3 (3a - 3b + 3c).\\] This results in $3ab + 3bc + 3ac + 3ab + 3ab + 3ab + 3bc + 3ac + 3bc + 3ab + 3bc + 3bc = 72$ and so it follows that \\[3(ab + ac + bc) = 72 - 3(3ab + 3bc + 3ac) + 3 + 3(ab + ac + bc).\\] This simplifies to $0 = 25,$ and so $ab + ac + bc = \\boxed{7}.$The answer is: 7",
